WEBVTT

00:00:02.294 --> 00:00:04.837
All right, you're right. Forget it.
The Dolphin job is off.

00:00:04.922 --> 00:00:06.047
Good.

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:08.341
I guess the pig
will get his trophy after all.

00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:09.926
Yeah, I guess he would...

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.387
What do you mean, "pig"?

00:00:12.471 --> 00:00:15.890
Yes, did I not mention that? That's weird.
I thought I mentioned that it was...

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.935
The Good Samaritan is...

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.186
A guinea pig?

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.021
[shuddering]

00:00:22.106 --> 00:00:23.648
What do you say, Snakey?

00:00:23.732 --> 00:00:24.982
Better than cake.

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:26.609
[laughing]

00:00:26.694 --> 00:00:29.362
[grunts] Okay. Fine.

00:00:29.446 --> 00:00:31.114
But he better be delicious.

00:00:31.198 --> 00:00:33.700
[laughs] Are we all in this together?

00:00:35.202 --> 00:00:36.661
<i>[Wolf] So, here's the plan.</i>

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:41.332
<i>Like every year, the ceremony will be held</i>
<i>at the Museum of Fine Arts,</i>

00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:43.668
<i>where the Golden Dolphin</i>
<i>will be positioned</i>

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:46.170
<i>just beyond the backstage curtain.</i>

00:00:46.255 --> 00:00:47.338
Sounds easy.

00:00:47.423 --> 00:00:48.923
Sounds easy, hermano.

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:52.176
But to get there, we'll need to bypass
three levels of security.

00:00:52.261 --> 00:00:53.261
So, step one.

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:55.430
<i>We'll need to blend in.</i>

00:00:56.348 --> 00:00:58.975
<i>♪ Baby, I'm howlin' for you ♪</i>

00:01:03.522 --> 00:01:07.066
<i>[Wolf] Professor Marmalade, this year's</i>
<i>recipient of the Golden Dolphin,</i>

00:01:07.151 --> 00:01:09.444
<i>the most annoying</i>
<i>good creature on the planet.</i>

00:01:09.528 --> 00:01:13.030
Professor, in the past year,
you've stopped wars, fed the hungry

00:01:13.115 --> 00:01:14.866
and saved countless pandas.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:18.786
Some have described your goodness
as second only to Mother Teresa.

00:01:18.871 --> 00:01:21.289
Oh, Tiffany.
It's not a competition.

00:01:21.373 --> 00:01:23.624
And if it were,
it would really be more of a tie.

00:01:23.709 --> 00:01:25.209
But we can all agree

00:01:25.294 --> 00:01:28.045
that there is a flower of goodness
inside all of us

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:30.006
just waiting to blossom.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.925
<i>[Wolf] Once inside,</i>
<i>there are two armored doors.</i>

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:36.053
<i>The first can only be opened</i>
<i>by a special key card</i>

00:01:36.138 --> 00:01:38.848
<i>that is carried by our dear friend,</i>
<i>the chief of police.</i>

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.642
<i>The second is outfitted</i>
<i>with a retinal scanner</i>

00:01:41.727 --> 00:01:43.519
<i>and guarded by an elite special-ops unit</i>

00:01:43.604 --> 00:01:46.314
<i>trained to strike first</i>
<i>and ask questions later.</i>

00:01:46.398 --> 00:01:47.398
[insect buzzing]

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:52.904
<i>[Wolf] Governor Foxington is the only one</i>
<i>who has clearance to open the second door.</i>

00:01:52.988 --> 00:01:56.407
<i>So, step two, she and I will need to</i>
<i>get up close and personal.</i>

00:01:56.992 --> 00:01:59.202
Enjoy your evening, Mr. Ambassador.

00:01:59.286 --> 00:02:00.912
[Wolf] Interesting piece.

00:02:00.996 --> 00:02:04.373
Trashy, pointless and pretentious.

00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:09.086
Hmm. They say that art reveals
more about the viewer than the artist.

00:02:09.171 --> 00:02:10.254
Mister...

00:02:10.339 --> 00:02:13.633
- Poodleton. Oliver Poodleton.
- Okay.

00:02:13.717 --> 00:02:18.471
It's about time someone stood up
to those diabolical Bad Guys.

00:02:18.555 --> 00:02:21.390
Though, I've got to say,
no one's succeeded yet.

00:02:21.475 --> 00:02:23.976
Eh. I don't think it'll be that hard.

00:02:24.061 --> 00:02:26.354
I have a feeling
it'll be harder than you think.

00:02:26.438 --> 00:02:29.774
I'd say they're one epic job away
from cementing their legacy.

00:02:32.903 --> 00:02:34.570
Mr. Poodleton. You're funny.

00:02:34.655 --> 00:02:35.863
I am?

00:02:35.948 --> 00:02:38.282
The only legacy they're cementing
is life in prison.

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:40.409
Did you see their last job?

00:02:40.494 --> 00:02:44.413
Ugh, unsecured exits, crude disguises,
compulsive showboating.

00:02:44.498 --> 00:02:45.832
I mean, it was a mess.

00:02:45.916 --> 00:02:48.668
All the classic signs
of a crew in decline.

00:02:48.752 --> 00:02:51.671
Next, they're gonna make it personal.

00:02:51.755 --> 00:02:54.048
That's when you know they're toast.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.844
Uh, well, that's your opinion.

00:02:57.928 --> 00:02:59.971
It is. And I'm the governor.

00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:04.767
As for the sculpture,
I think it's about perspective.

00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:07.311
If you look closely enough,

00:03:07.396 --> 00:03:10.565
even trash can be recycled
into something beautiful.

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:14.110
[Wolf] How about that.

00:03:14.945 --> 00:03:17.738
I guess some things
aren't always as they appear.

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:20.616
That reminds me, may I?

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:23.995
I can't miss a photo op with the governor
and a pile of garbage.

00:03:24.079 --> 00:03:26.914
Mr. Poodleton,
you're too hard on yourself.

00:03:26.999 --> 00:03:28.040
Hey...

00:03:29.877 --> 00:03:31.210
[guests chattering]

00:03:31.295 --> 00:03:32.587
Okay, friends.

00:03:32.671 --> 00:03:34.422
It's showtime.

00:03:36.341 --> 00:03:38.509
[Wolf] Once we're in,
<i>it's on to step three.</i>

00:03:38.594 --> 00:03:40.553
<i>We split up and we take our positions.</i>

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:44.891
Officers, if the Bad Guys
crash this event,

00:03:44.975 --> 00:03:46.726
I am definitely going to lose my job.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:50.479
And I will not hesitate to
take you down with me.

00:03:50.564 --> 00:03:51.647
Now, move out!

00:03:51.732 --> 00:03:53.149
[officers] Yes, ma'am!
Hut, hut, hut, hut!

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.526
Hut, hut, hut, hut, hut,
hut, hut, hut, hut, hut!

00:04:10.292 --> 00:04:12.543
Mic's on.
Everyone on comms, do you copy?

00:04:12.628 --> 00:04:13.628
- Copy.
- Copy.

00:04:13.712 --> 00:04:15.087
- Copy.
- Copy.

00:04:23.597 --> 00:04:25.306
[Snake laughing]

00:04:34.232 --> 00:04:35.650
A drink for the pretty lady?

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:39.028
No, thank you.
My life is too complicated right now.

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:40.112
Uh...

00:04:42.532 --> 00:04:44.951
[groans, gags]

00:05:07.557 --> 00:05:09.642
Boys, it's dolphin season.

00:05:09.726 --> 00:05:10.768
[muffled mumbling]

00:05:12.562 --> 00:05:14.230
Copy that. I'm on the move.

00:05:16.233 --> 00:05:18.484
Unit Two,
is the backstage area still secure?

00:05:18.568 --> 00:05:19.652
<i>[officer] Unit Two. All clear.</i>

00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:21.946
This is where all the training pays off.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:24.240
- [grunts, groans]
- Pardon me. Terribly sorry.

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:25.866
Not a problem, sir.

00:05:25.951 --> 00:05:27.785
Keep your eyes open, boys.

00:05:27.869 --> 00:05:31.163
They could be anywhere,
just waiting to humiliate us.

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:34.125
[Wolf laughs]

00:05:34.209 --> 00:05:35.751
Wolf is in position.

00:05:35.836 --> 00:05:38.462
<i>Piranha,</i>
<i>you all penguin-suited and booted?</i>

00:05:38.547 --> 00:05:42.258
Affirmative. I'm a clean, mean
dolphin-stealin' machine.

00:05:42.342 --> 00:05:43.676
What's goin' on, guys?

00:05:47.139 --> 00:05:49.140
[guests chattering]

